Drop the numba stack from the dx extras

The `cuNN-dx` extras pull in `nvmath-python[numba]`, which installs numba-cuda
(unused by the numba-cuda-mlir backend) and a released numba-cuda-mlir that
would shadow the wheel built by this CI run. Reduce the `numba` extra to cffi,
which the numba-cuda-mlir device modules import; everything else in it exists
only to support numba-cuda.

numba itself is dropped rather than kept, because nvmath's backend probe would
otherwise match numba's own `numba/cuda` shim - see
0001-disable-numba-cuda-backend.patch.

This keeps `pip install <checkout>[cuNN-dx]` as the single install command, so
the rest of the dx dependency set stays in sync with upstream.

Applied by ci/tools/run-nvmath-python-mlir-tests.

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -115,11 +115,6 @@ cu13 = [
 ]
 numba = [
     "cffi",
-    "llvmlite",
-    # numba-cuda defines version restriction
-    "numba",
-    "numba-cuda >=0.30.0, <1",
-    "numba-cuda-mlir >=0.4.1, <1; python_version >= '3.11'",
 ]
 sysctk12-dx = [
     "nvmath-python[sysctk12]",
